From 8dfcac3d536f0ec420f0c99b18f9417e496b5ba5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:03:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scripts: Run QEMU regression through regression.sh

Fold the QEMU suite list from scripts/regression-qemu.sh into
scripts/regression.sh behind CONFIG=qemu and remove the separate script,
so every platform is run through one regression entry point (#320).

The QEMU path runs the same eight suites in the same order, keeps the
previous defaults (RTE_IP=127.0.0.1, SNIPEIT_NO=no), and needs neither
FW_FILE nor DEVICE_IP. Other CONFIG values take the unchanged full path.
Extra arguments are forwarded to each robot run.

Document the unified command in docs/qemu.md.

Closes #320
---
 docs/qemu.md               |  8 ++++++++
 scripts/regression-qemu.sh | 38 --------------------------------------
 scripts/regression.sh      | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100755 scripts/regression-qemu.sh

diff --git a/docs/qemu.md b/docs/qemu.md
index 6f8373f..67b59f6 100644
--- a/docs/qemu.md
+++ b/docs/qemu.md
@@ -67,6 +67,14 @@ robot -b command_log.txt -v snipeit:no -L TRACE -v config:qemu -v rte_ip:127.0.0
 > is being used. Use QEMU config `-v config:qemu`, and, as a RTE IP, use
 > `127.0.0.1`. Test suite `dts/dts-tests.robot` is shown here as an example.
 
+To run the QEMU-capable compatibility and security suites in one command, set
+`CONFIG=qemu` and use the shared regression wrapper. It needs no firmware file
+or device IP, and it sets `RTE_IP=127.0.0.1` itself:
+
+```bash
+CONFIG=qemu ./scripts/regression.sh
+```
+
 ## Connecting to the machine
 
 The machine's serial port is available over Telnet on `127.0.0.1:1234`.
